Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/pull/11079
  "font/shaper: add RTL shaping for Arabic and Hebrew" (open, unmerged)

Arabic-script text — Persian included — needs two things a terminal
usually lacks: contextual letterforms, so letters join, and a visual
order, so a line reads right to left. libghostty has neither, which
renders Farsi as disconnected letters running backwards.

This adds both at the shaper: uucode supplies bidi classes, itijah
(UAX #9) resolves each run's visual order, and the CoreText and
HarfBuzz shapers consume the run direction.

Carried here because it is unmerged upstream. Drop this file when the
pin reaches a commit that already has it.

